    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode` \u2014 as a derived, read-only field on the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer, 0\u20139, `readOnly`), placed right after `customerCode`. This generates the field on the `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` default method implementing the standard Luhn algorithm over the digit characters of the customer code (returns `null` when `customerCode` is absent, mirroring the existing `membershipNumber` convention).\n\nThe implementation deliberately mirrors the reference `luhn(String)` in `AcceptanceBase` exactly (iterate right-to-left, doubling from the first processed digit, skipping non-digits), so the recomputed value matches the returned one. `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nOne note: the OpenAPI description for `customerCode` says `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, but the actual `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` produces `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`. That's a pre-existing doc/code discrepancy unrelated to this change \u2014 the Luhn computation operates on whatever digits the code contains, so it's correct either way.",
