        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change drops cleanly into the existing shape of this mapper:\n\n- `OwnerMapper` already hosts a family of small `default` derivation helpers for computed DTO fields (`contactPreference`, `locality`, `membershipNumber`). `checkDigit(Owner owner)` is exactly this kind of unit \u2014 single derivation, self-contained, invoked via the same `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(...)\")` convention. The logic is in the right place; this file *is* the home for owner-derived fields.\n- It matches local conventions: same `default X foo(Owner owner)` signature shape, same null-when-source-absent guard as `membershipNumber`, same Javadoc style. It's placed directly beside `membershipNumber`, the other customerCode-derived helper \u2014 a maintainer would find it where they'd expect.\n- No duplication: although both `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` read `customerCode`, they compute unrelated things and share no extractable logic. The Luhn loop is a single cohesive algorithm, not something to split.\n- Not a catch-all growth: the mapper gains one more field helper consistent with the three already present, not an unrelated responsibility.\n- The OpenAPI schema addition (`readOnly`, bounded 0\u20139 integer, description noting it's derived from the owner's own fields) is consistent with the sibling read-only derived properties.\n\nNo structural changes warranted."
